{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-31eb-7305-8b3a-d39b8710f340","id":"01a1a662-b05d-77bd-b366-99deb66ac271","idempotency_key":"a7dc648d57189856aa049e4991f9d6629bcb27923e6ef76b5c17fbc8965ba97b","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:47:27Z","payload":{"episode":0,"item":"i-256c","note":"POST /api/studies/import-pgn: a Lichess study export is PGN with numbered chapters, so one game becomes one chapter with its Event as the title and its movetext as the board. Verified with a two-game PGN -> two chapters.","on":"2026-11-04","target":"t-2927/i-256c"},"type":"work.item_done","v":2}
{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-31eb-7305-8b3a-d39b8710f340","id":"01a1a662-b070-7470-8c24-e7d732013a2c","idempotency_key":"4d353193ea2795033f10a983be81c223afaeda8a7eec43cb2914d57f054b26a9","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:47:27Z","payload":{"episode":0,"item":"i-c1c9","note":"Unknown top-level, chapter and board fields are kept in Bundle.other and written back by to_json; a test proves a future_field survives a parse/write cycle.","on":"2026-11-04","target":"t-2927/i-c1c9"},"type":"work.item_done","v":2}
{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-31eb-7305-8b3a-d39b8710f340","id":"01a1a662-b081-7243-b779-9eb92d71d5f6","idempotency_key":"2433b6850eb25bebfc10d5f7fdfbb1057b36901450100db45863b122e1811ac4","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:47:28Z","payload":{"episode":0,"item":"i-e7f2","note":"6 tests in crates/ai/tests/study_bundle.rs: lossless round trip, unknown-field survival, refusal of a non-bundle, lineage in the bundle, and a full import into a different database.","on":"2026-11-04","target":"t-2927/i-e7f2"},"type":"work.item_done","v":2}
{"actor_ref":"claude","class":"draft_history","document_uuid":"01a1a54a-31eb-7305-8b3a-d39b8710f340","id":"01a1a662-c766-719b-a6b7-21f246d823c4","idempotency_key":"b00f6d49b26950bbe5cf2d6043ee0d5ca0a3cce89bdb0359d896afbb264396e8","occurred_at":"2026-11-04T11:47:33Z","payload":{"note":"Closed 5/5. crates/ai/src/study_bundle.rs writes and reads the rbc-study/1 document the design fixes: schema, title, description, tags, lineage, chapters with their boards, notes, and lua null (R2). Each board travels as one PGN game with the study and chapter in its headers and a FEN header when the position is not the start. Unknown fields are KEPT at all three levels (top, chapter, board) in Bundle.other and written back by to_json - an old build editing a bundle must not silently delete a field a newer build wrote, and a test proves a future_field survives a parse/write cycle. GET /api/studies/{id}/bundle downloads one with content-disposition; POST /api/studies/import creates a study from one and reports chapters, boards and which fields it did not understand; POST /api/studies/import-pgn is the Lichess adapter, since a Lichess study export is PGN with the chapters numbered - one game becomes one chapter with its Event tag as the title and its movetext as the board (verified: a two-game PGN became 'Chapter 1: the Italian' and 'Chapter 2: the Sicilian' with 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 and 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6). Six tests. Two fixture mistakes of mine, both caught by the tests: add_chapter creates a board of its own so a chapter has one board before you add any, and '1. e4 e5 2. Nf3' does not contain the substring 'e4 e5 Nf3' because the movetext carries move numbers - the assertion compares SAN tokens now. Deliberately not done: fetching a study from lichess.org needs a token and a network call, which belongs with provider settings rather than an import that must work offline.","target":"t-2927"},"type":"work.note_added","v":2}
